WEBVTT

01:30.520 --> 01:33.480
Episode 10: Sweet Memory (Part 2)

01:37.980 --> 01:42.910
Don't worry. No one will find out what I did.

01:45.750 --> 01:50.630
And to make sure of it, 
I used Sanae-san to spread the idea

01:50.630 --> 01:55.550
that they might be able to make 
some money if they abduct me.

01:57.380 --> 02:01.300
It was also my idea to have Sanae-san 
bring the voice changer.

02:02.470 --> 02:06.350
It has Isawa-san's and 
everyone else's fingerprints on it.

02:18.070 --> 02:22.780
They're probably blaming each other for 
having brought the thing right about now.

02:23.490 --> 02:27.290
It doesn't matter if they 
find out it was mine, either.

02:27.580 --> 02:35.000
I've made sure that Sanae-san believes 
<i>she</i> was the one who came up with the plan.

02:38.420 --> 02:42.800
Besides, this irrefutable 
evidence will protect me.

02:43.300 --> 02:46.470
I was simply being threatened by Sanae-san.

02:46.930 --> 02:49.440
You can't treat crime 
like snacks, Osanai-san.

02:52.270 --> 02:55.020
You can't frame people for crimes
they didn't commit.

02:55.520 --> 02:58.440
This is wrong. This is a lie.

02:58.860 --> 03:02.950
You even used me and 
Kawamata Sanae to your own ends.

03:03.410 --> 03:06.950
We were made accomplices to your lie.

03:08.000 --> 03:09.460
This is really bad, Osanai-san.

03:10.540 --> 03:13.710
I don't know how deep your hatred 
for Isawa Hasemi's gang runs,

03:13.710 --> 03:17.590
but no matter how you try 
to spin it, this is a terrible lie.

03:18.210 --> 03:19.550
You're a liar.

03:33.520 --> 03:36.110
I'm a liar?

03:36.650 --> 03:37.730
That's right.

03:48.700 --> 03:52.040
I see. I'm a liar.

03:52.870 --> 03:56.380
I lied to you and Dojima-kun.

03:58.130 --> 04:02.680
I broke our promise of 
becoming ordinary spectacularly.

04:05.260 --> 04:06.390
But you know...

04:07.390 --> 04:09.890
So did you.

04:10.850 --> 04:15.100
The way you interrogated me just now...

04:15.100 --> 04:17.020
You seemed to be enjoying it.

04:19.230 --> 04:22.070
You lie about not wanting 
to solve mysteries.

04:23.070 --> 04:26.740
In other words, 
your trying to become ordinary is also a lie.

04:26.740 --> 04:27.660
Well...

04:28.240 --> 04:32.410
Everyone thinks we're in a relationship.

04:33.330 --> 04:35.080
But that's a lie, too.

04:35.080 --> 04:39.380
Everyone at school says I'm really quiet.

04:39.380 --> 04:42.970
You're just a pretty smile. A safe choice.

04:43.550 --> 04:44.800
But that's a lie, too.

04:44.800 --> 04:47.300
Lies here, lies there.

04:50.810 --> 04:52.890
But there's one thing that's not a lie.

04:53.560 --> 04:57.310
I never really wanted to do this.

04:58.360 --> 05:05.820
Yet you have no idea why 
I chose to do things this way.

05:06.410 --> 05:08.240
You don't even try to understand.

05:09.700 --> 05:12.370
I was scared.

05:13.000 --> 05:16.080
Knowing what Isawa-san could do to me,

05:16.080 --> 05:19.080
I wanted to keep her away from me
 for as long as I could.

05:20.040 --> 05:23.340
So I got her to become a kidnapper.

05:24.210 --> 05:29.600
If what I did was a lie, it was a lie to 
run away from someone who scared me.

05:30.180 --> 05:35.140
But you would never 
have understood that lie.

05:35.640 --> 05:40.360
Because all you're ever 
capable of is thinking.

05:44.740 --> 05:46.450
I disappoint myself, too.

05:47.030 --> 05:49.740
You saw through my lie and my plan.

05:51.080 --> 05:55.790
If we aren't a pair of intelligent 
foxes or wolves or anything...

05:57.000 --> 06:01.840
If our desire to become 
ordinary is also a lie...

06:02.500 --> 06:04.000
Then, what's left of us?

06:04.840 --> 06:07.010
Can you guess?

06:11.140 --> 06:12.510
What's left...

06:13.760 --> 06:17.520
is just two arrogant high schoolers.

06:18.940 --> 06:24.150
Just as I'd first suspected, 
a timetable was the key to this problem.

06:25.110 --> 06:30.820
Using in-line skates for your alibi 
wasn't <i>entirely</i> original,

06:30.820 --> 06:32.620
but it wasn't a bad idea.

06:33.280 --> 06:36.040
You chose the wrong person 
to try to use it on, though.

06:36.830 --> 06:42.670
Remember the bassist's disappearance? 
I was the one who solved that mystery.

06:43.290 --> 06:50.050
Yes, it was I who had Sagawa 
and his friends taken into custody.

06:50.680 --> 06:56.850
And in this case, I'm not afraid to state
that you were the one who set her up.

06:59.270 --> 07:01.350
Well? Do you admit defeat?

07:01.350 --> 07:05.770
Or are you going to waste 
everyone's time with pointless excuses?

07:08.360 --> 07:12.780
But you know, it isn't too late 
to make up for what you did.

07:12.780 --> 07:19.040
If you have even a speck of honesty left,
 that's what you should do.

07:22.290 --> 07:23.080
Wow.

07:23.080 --> 07:25.290
That makes sense.

07:24.590 --> 07:26.580
I can't believe he was behind it.

07:25.290 --> 07:27.130
Amazing.

07:27.130 --> 07:28.600
That's Kobato Jogoro.

07:28.600 --> 07:30.510
Fantastic!

07:30.510 --> 07:33.970
That was a truly elegant solution.

07:34.350 --> 07:36.010
A beautiful proof.

07:36.010 --> 07:40.480
But I don't know how to say this...

07:41.560 --> 07:47.980
To be completely blunt, 
you're kind of annoying.

07:47.980 --> 07:50.110
Annoying.

07:49.280 --> 07:51.070
Annoying.

07:51.820 --> 07:53.900
Hey, Kobato-kun.

07:55.660 --> 07:59.370
There's no point in us 
being together anymore.

08:00.790 --> 08:08.170
The deal was to lend each other a hand 
so that we could become ordinary.

08:08.960 --> 08:11.300
We'd avoid getting caught up
 in people's problems,

08:11.630 --> 08:13.800
and make sure to live normal lives.

08:14.220 --> 08:19.430
You'd shield me, and I'd shield you.

08:20.560 --> 08:26.020
So that no one would point fingers at us.

08:27.770 --> 08:34.490
That promise seemed absolutely necessary 
for us as middle schoolers.

08:35.570 --> 08:38.580
I think it was, too.

08:39.280 --> 08:40.160
But...

08:41.950 --> 08:43.960
We've done enough.

08:50.170 --> 08:56.050
We say we're ordinary, 
but we don't actually think we are.

08:56.890 --> 09:00.350
We say we wish we were ordinary,

09:00.810 --> 09:05.390
but we aren't really even 
thinking about becoming ordinary.

09:08.730 --> 09:13.820
As long as the two of us are together,
 that'll never change.

09:15.110 --> 09:16.570
Don't you agree?

09:20.950 --> 09:21.910
You're right.

09:22.290 --> 09:27.540
I play detective the most when I'm with you.

09:28.000 --> 09:30.540
I have to concede I was hiding behind you.

09:31.590 --> 09:32.800
Me, too.

09:33.210 --> 09:36.300
I kept telling myself it'd be fine 
because you'd be there.

09:48.810 --> 09:53.440
Still, I don't agree that there's 
no reason for us to stick together.

09:54.190 --> 09:58.030
Although I agree our arrangement
 isn't effective anymore.

09:59.280 --> 10:02.200
I suspected you'd answer that way.

10:02.200 --> 10:04.080
It's the only possible answer.

10:04.080 --> 10:05.290
I don't mean that.

10:05.750 --> 10:07.750
I don't mean what you're saying.

10:07.750 --> 10:09.710
I mean how you're responding.

10:10.710 --> 10:14.670
I'm talking about breaking it off with you.

10:14.670 --> 10:19.260
If "breaking it off" sounds 
too much like we're dating,

10:19.260 --> 10:21.720
I mean we should 
terminate our relationship.

10:22.760 --> 10:28.020
I'm sure you can figure out why 
I wouldn't have brought it up until now,

10:28.020 --> 10:30.560
if that's what I've been 
thinking all this time.

10:31.310 --> 10:37.360
Because we couldn't separate 
until we'd dealt with Isawa Hasemi.

10:38.070 --> 10:39.240
Right.

10:39.530 --> 10:42.070
Don't you think that's selfish of me?

10:42.490 --> 10:47.040
Even though you were angry 
that I'd lied and framed Isawa-san?

10:47.040 --> 10:49.750
You broke the rules. Of course I was.

10:54.960 --> 11:00.630
But I'm in no position to be angry
 at you for having used me.

11:01.010 --> 11:05.140
See? We can't even quarrel.

11:06.390 --> 11:10.940
We're sitting here trying to assess 
what was correct or necessary.

11:11.900 --> 11:15.150
All we can do is think.

11:15.150 --> 11:18.320
We don't get angry, 
and we don't get sad at all.

11:21.240 --> 11:26.120
I just finished a homework assignment 
from middle school today.

11:28.200 --> 11:30.540
I think it's the right time.

11:53.310 --> 11:55.860
I understand what you're trying to say.

11:59.030 --> 12:00.500
Let's go our separate ways.

12:03.530 --> 12:05.780
I'm sorry, Kobato-kun.

12:15.710 --> 12:16.840
But...

12:18.420 --> 12:20.970
Our sweets tour together...

12:21.800 --> 12:24.430
I'd be lying if I said 
I didn't enjoy it at all.

13:30.330 --> 13:35.210
High School Students Abduct One of Their Own for Money

13:30.330 --> 13:35.210
<b>Kira News</b>

13:30.330 --> 13:35.210
m 0 0 l 97 0 100 100 1 100

13:30.330 --> 13:35.210
<b>The Kira City Police Department took into custody
five female high school students under suspicion of
abducting and assaulting a fellow female student
and demanding a ransom from her family.</b>

13:30.330 --> 13:35.210
<b>Read article</b>

13:42.710 --> 13:48.720
<b>Unexpected</b>

13:50.720 --> 13:58.230
<b>Salt flavor</b>

13:50.720 --> 13:58.230
<b>Caramel flavor</b>

13:50.720 --> 13:58.230
<b>Chocolate flavor</b>

14:01.230 --> 14:03.230
Sheesh, Kenken.

14:06.740 --> 14:07.820
Does this work?

14:07.820 --> 14:08.660
Yeah.

14:08.660 --> 14:10.120
This one, please.

14:55.160 --> 14:56.250
All right.

15:17.680 --> 15:21.980
After class, 5:30 PM

15:17.680 --> 15:21.980
Please come to the

15:17.680 --> 15:21.980
classroom alone

15:17.680 --> 15:21.980
I'll be waiting

15:17.680 --> 15:21.980
Nakamaru

15:40.790 --> 15:43.750
And 5:30 on the dot. 
You sure are punctual.

15:45.460 --> 15:47.500
You did call for me, after all.

15:57.850 --> 16:00.930
You broke up with that girl, didn't you?

16:01.520 --> 16:03.100
What's wrong?

16:03.100 --> 16:05.110
You don't need to be so shocked.

16:06.860 --> 16:10.780
I'm not shocked exactly.
I'm just wondering how you knew.

16:13.160 --> 16:15.450
It's pretty obvious.

16:15.450 --> 16:19.330
I haven't seen you two together once
since summer break ended.

16:21.210 --> 16:22.370
Yeah?

16:23.170 --> 16:24.750
I guess it is easy to tell, huh?

16:25.170 --> 16:27.460
So you did break up, then.

16:27.460 --> 16:29.460
Yeah. We did.

16:29.710 --> 16:31.590
Wanna go out with me, then?

16:33.010 --> 16:34.390
Let's do this.

16:39.470 --> 16:44.140
Hey, your first name's Jogoro, right?

16:44.600 --> 16:46.110
Can I call you "Jo"?

16:46.110 --> 16:47.230
No.

16:47.230 --> 16:48.690
Okay, it's settled.

16:49.110 --> 16:51.190
I'm looking forward to this, Kobato.

16:52.440 --> 16:54.950
Please come to the

16:52.440 --> 16:54.950
classroom alone

16:52.440 --> 16:54.950
Nakamaru Tokiko

16:56.450 --> 16:59.120
Am I really that off-base?

16:59.120 --> 17:00.700
It's on the news online.

17:00.700 --> 17:02.580
There <i>are</i> people who know about it.

17:03.160 --> 17:05.580
So why not?

17:06.330 --> 17:09.250
This club makes a campus newsletter,

17:09.250 --> 17:11.210
not a "local news" section.

17:11.800 --> 17:15.220
Does it look like we have the 
resources to interview the police?

17:15.590 --> 17:17.970
Can we ask the victim to comment?

17:17.970 --> 17:22.350
Who's going to be responsible 
if someone gets into trouble?

17:22.350 --> 17:25.520
Your parents? Our advisory teacher, Miyoshi?

17:25.520 --> 17:26.730
Or me?

17:28.150 --> 17:33.440
If there's something you really want 
the public to know, go post it anonymously.

17:33.440 --> 17:35.650
I'm telling you, I have information...

17:35.110 --> 17:39.620
High School Students Abduct One of Their Own for Money

17:35.650 --> 17:39.620
that the student abducted in 
this article goes to our school.

17:40.080 --> 17:43.660
This has to do with our school. 
So why is it off limits?

17:46.370 --> 17:48.710
Enough. This is a presidential decision.

17:49.170 --> 17:51.300
But if you want, we can hold a vote.

17:58.510 --> 18:00.050
Fine.

18:01.180 --> 18:02.280
It's true, though.

18:02.280 --> 18:05.390
Our club's activities are pretty boring.

18:05.390 --> 18:09.520
Right? There's nothing to do 
other than copy last year's articles.

18:10.400 --> 18:13.400
That's why I told you 
it'd be a waste of time.

18:17.910 --> 18:23.410
You're the type that doesn't do things you
 think are a waste. I'm the type that does.

18:23.410 --> 18:24.830
That's mighty admirable of you.

18:25.870 --> 18:26.920
All right, then, Hiya...

18:27.790 --> 18:30.790
You went to middle school 
for three years, too, right?

18:31.290 --> 18:32.290
Yeah.

18:32.290 --> 18:34.920
Did you ever do anything noteworthy?

18:36.920 --> 18:38.260
I didn't.

18:38.760 --> 18:41.800
I studied, went to club meets,
 and that was it.

18:42.900 --> 18:49.520
I don't want three more years of the same.
 I decided that nearly six months ago.

18:50.380 --> 18:53.700
And your solution to that was 
to join the newspaper club?

18:58.320 --> 19:01.440
Well, I'll be rooting for you.
 You can count on it.

19:03.950 --> 19:06.950
<b>History of Science</b>

19:03.950 --> 19:06.950
<b>Happy
Daifuku</b>

19:03.950 --> 19:06.950
On Writing Good Articles

19:03.950 --> 19:06.950
<b>How To Listen</b>

19:29.820 --> 19:31.320
Did you need something from me?

19:31.320 --> 19:32.630
Oh, no, uh...

19:33.130 --> 19:34.310
Um, sorry.

19:35.550 --> 19:39.000
Have I seen you somewhere before?

19:39.000 --> 19:42.580
Oh, I think we met in the newspaper club.

19:42.810 --> 19:44.280
The newspaper club?

19:48.460 --> 19:50.040
I don't remember.

19:51.810 --> 19:52.650
I'm sorry.

19:52.650 --> 19:56.750
Oh, uh, it's fine. We didn't talk,
 so I don't blame you.

20:02.120 --> 20:03.890
So, did you need something from me?

20:03.890 --> 20:05.210
Oh, no, uh...

20:10.010 --> 20:11.280
You caught my eye...

20:12.260 --> 20:13.980
the moment I saw you.

20:13.980 --> 20:16.750
If you have some time, could we chat?

20:16.750 --> 20:18.410
I've been wanting to talk to you.

20:41.100 --> 20:45.670
I think I kind of like 
straightforward boys.

20:47.190 --> 20:48.310
Sure.

20:48.820 --> 20:51.680
I don't want to chat in the library, though.

20:52.060 --> 20:53.960
I know a nice shop.

20:53.960 --> 20:56.740
They do a delicious strawberry cake there.

20:56.740 --> 20:58.200
Let's go, then.
